*.pdf

# The web frontend's output (`suzatary web site`). Generated from the chain,
# and regenerable in a second — committing it would be a second
# copy of the history to keep in step with the first.
/site/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Agent worktrees. These are meant to be transient: a subagent gets one, does its job,
# its work is merged, and the worktree goes away. Ignoring them is a guard, not the
# policy — a worktree that is live *during* a subagent run would otherwise trip
# safe-push.sh's allowlist and silently block the unattended triage agent from pushing
# anything at all, and that race shouldn't depend on nobody having a subagent open.
# Sweeping them when the subagent finishes is still the expectation:
#   git worktree remove <path> && git worktree prune && git branch -D worktree-<id>
# Check `git log master..worktree-<id>` AND the worktree's untracked files first. The
# two swept on 2026-08-06 sat on commits already in master but each still held an
# untracked candidates-*.md that existed nowhere else until it was copied out by hand —
# "its commits are merged" is not the same as "it holds nothing."
.claude/worktrees/

# The web app's bundle, and the fixtures it can be developed against. Both are
# builds: `scripts/build-web.sh` writes web/dist/ from web/src + web/static +
# the flake's prodrome-wasm, and `scripts/web-fixtures.py` writes web/dev/ from
# the chain. The repository releases the program, not its output.
web/dist/
web/dev/

# The application's build directory (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §2, the `app/`
# workspace — the only one here since the database became its own repository,
# §8.8, which is why `prodrome/target/` is no longer a line above this one).
# Same rule as web/dist/: cargo writes it from app/*/src, and it is
# output, not source. `app/Cargo.lock` IS committed — the workspace's
# deliverable is a binary, and one of its dependencies is a git revision, so the
# dependency set is pinned twice over.
app/target/
# Any side target (a session building master beside its branch committed
# 724 MB of one, app/target-master/, on 2026-09-29).
app/target-*/

# The wire's TypeScript, generated from app/core/src/wire.rs by
# `nix build .#suzatary-wire-ts` and copied in by scripts/build-web.sh. Output,
# not source — committing it would be the second declaration ARCHITECTURE §2
# exists to prevent, kept in step by hand.
web/src/wire/generated/

# proptest's shrunk counterexamples. A cache of seeds, not source: this repo
# has never tracked one, and a checked-in case from an agent's own development
# would pin the generator it happened to have that afternoon.
proptest-regressions/

# The secretary's conversations (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §10.3). BOX-LOCAL, like
# the maildir and unlike `events/`: a transcript quotes mail, and mail is never
# committed. It is not rebuildable either, which makes it the one piece of state
# here that only this box has — said out loud rather than discovered.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and that is not decoration: a bare `secretary/`
# matches a directory of that name ANYWHERE, and `app/core/src/secretary/` is a
# module. The unanchored pattern silently untracked a source file the moment it
# was written — caught the same afternoon, by `git status` not listing it.
/secretary/
/decisions/

# A turn's rendered SVGs (`docs/APP.md`, "typstanswers") — a SIBLING of
# `/secretary/` above and gitignored the same way, for the same reasons: it is
# box-local and it is not rebuildable state's opposite — a DERIVED cache keyed
# by the sha256 of a turn's own text, so it is never source. Kept OUT of
# `/secretary/` rather than nested under it so a rendering can never be
# mistaken for a line of the append-only transcript.
/secretary-render/

# The inbox prodrome (`docs/PROPOSALS-PLAN-2026-09-28.md`): every proposal and
# what became of it, box-local like `/secretary/`, whose drafts it quotes.
/inbox/

# THE DATA LIVES IN ITS OWN REPOSITORY (datasplit, 2026-09-26): the private
# data repository, checked out beside this one. `instance.toml` here is
# a link to that tree's file, so a command run from this checkout reads the
# same deployment the units do. Nothing below is ever committed here again.
/instance.toml
/mbsyncrc
/state.json
/events/
/events-suzatary/
/briefings/
/notes/
/secretary/
/decisions/

# THE CACHE TIER (docs/PLUGINS-PLAN-2026-10-02.md §4): the plugins' stores, cursors and
# ledgers under the data root's `cache/`, a replica of outside truths rebuilt by syncing
# again. Box-local, never pushed; the data repository ignores it the same way.
/cache/
